# Generated Tree-sitter parsers.
#
# These are committed on purpose — the build must not need Node — but they are
# machine output, not source: a diff of one is thousands of lines of state tables
# that no one can read, and a merge of two is never resolvable by hand. Marking
# them `linguist-generated` keeps them out of language statistics and collapses
# them in review; `-diff` stops Git printing them; `-merge` makes a conflict fail
# loudly so it is settled by regenerating the grammar, which is the only correct
# resolution.
#
# Picus's is the extreme case at ~32 MB (a full SQL + PL/SQL grammar parsed to
# expression depth); Merula's and Bennu's are a couple of hundred KB.
**/src/parser.c   linguist-generated=true -diff -merge
**/src/grammar.json      linguist-generated=true -diff -merge
**/src/node-types.json   linguist-generated=true -diff -merge
